From: Joseph Telaak <joseph@telaak.dev>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/gma500: Leave memory self-refresh off on Cedarview

With a single pipe on, cdv_update_wm() programs fixed FIFO watermarks
and turns on memory self-refresh. The watermarks come from neither the
mode nor the memory's self-refresh exit latency.

On two Cedarview laptops this blacks out the LVDS panel, with the
backlight still on:
- Atom N2600 (Coradir ES10IS5, 1024x600): the panel goes black when the
  GPU starts using memory. With self-refresh left off, the same GPU
  work runs with the panel up.
- Atom D2500 (Philco 14H): on the boots that come up black, pipe B runs
  (PIPEBCONF bit 30 is set) and its FIFO underrun bit is set. A full
  modeset doesn't clear it.

With self-refresh left off, the underrun bit stayed clear from boot
through GPU work and X's start in all twelve test boots, six on each
laptop.

Leave self-refresh off. Every DPMS change still runs cdv_disable_sr()
first, so self-refresh that the firmware left on gets turned off.
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/gma500/cdv_intel_display.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/gma500/cdv_intel_display.c
@@ -530,11 +530,10 @@ void cdv_update_wm(struct drm_device *dev, struct drm_crtc *crtc)
 
 		REG_WRITE(DSPFW6, 0x10);
 
-		gma_wait_for_vblank(dev);
-
-		/* enable self-refresh for single pipe active */
-		REG_WRITE(FW_BLC_SELF, FW_BLC_SELF_EN);
-		REG_READ(FW_BLC_SELF);
+		/*
+		 * Memory self-refresh stays off: these fixed watermarks don't
+		 * cover its exit latency, and the pipe's FIFO underruns.
+		 */
 		gma_wait_for_vblank(dev);
 
 	} else {
